## Per-Topic Content Outline

### 1 — GCP project and APIs

- Create/select project `boutique-gke`; link billing
- Enable APIs: `container`, `compute`, `dns`, `iam`, `artifactregistry`, `secretmanager`, `monitoring`, `logging`, `cloudtrace`, `binaryauthorization`, `iap` (if used)
- Set default region/zone; configure `gcloud config`

### 2 — Terraform remote state

- GCS bucket with versioning + uniform access
- State prefix: `boutique/terraform.tfstate`
- Optional: DynamoDB-style locking via GCS (Terraform 1.x native locking) or document lock mechanism
- `backend.tf` in `terraform/environments/boutique/`

### 3 — VPC, subnets, Cloud NAT

- Custom VPC; private subnet for nodes; secondary ranges for pods/services
- Cloud Router + Cloud NAT for private node egress
- Private Google Access enabled
- Firewall: allow health checks; deny broad ingress

### 4 — GKE cluster

- Regional private cluster; Workload Identity enabled
- Multi-zone node pool; autoscaling min/max
- Authorized networks or IAP for admin access
- `kubectl get-credentials` validation

### 5 — Cloud DNS + NS delegation

- Managed zone for `biroltilki.art` or subdomain strategy
- A records: `boutique`, `argocd` → static IP (may be created in topic 6)
- Registrar NS delegation steps (UI detailed)
- See also [docs/dns.md](../dns.md)

### 6 — Static ingress IP + TLS

- Reserve global static IP (Terraform)
- GCE Ingress annotations; Google-managed certificates
- Map DNS A records; wait for cert provisioning (can take 15–60 min)
- `curl -I` both hostnames

### 7 — GitHub WIF → GCP

- Terraform `wif` module: pool, OIDC provider, attribute mapping
- GitHub repo settings: allow OIDC, restrict to repo/ref
- GitHub Actions workflow snippet: `google-github-actions/auth`
- **No JSON key download** — security notes mandatory

### 8 — Artifact Registry + Binary Authorization

- AR repository; cleanup/retention policy
- Attestor + policy (require attestation from CI SA)
- Test push from local or dry-run workflow

### 9 — Argo CD bootstrap

- Install via Helm or `gitops/bootstrap/argocd/`
- Ingress for `argocd.boutique.biroltilki.art`
- Admin password retrieval; disable or SSO note for prod
- App-of-apps `root-app.yaml`

### 10 — ESO + Secret Manager

- Install ESO operator; `ClusterSecretStore` for GCP SM
- Workload Identity binding for ESO K8s SA
- Sample `ExternalSecret` (no real secret values in Git)

### 11 — Kyverno policies

- Install Kyverno; apply five minimum policies
- Policy tests in `tests/kyverno/`
- Verify deny on `:latest` test manifest

### 12 — Online Boutique deploy

- Helm chart in `gitops/apps/boutique/`
- Digest-only `values-images.yaml`
- Argo Application; **manual sync**
- Binary Auth + Kyverno must pass

### 13 — Observability + SLOs

- OTel Collector → Cloud Trace + Managed Prometheus
- Grafana dashboards; datasource config
- Cloud Monitoring SLOs: browse 99.9%, checkout 99.95%
- Burn-rate alert policies with runbook URLs

### 14 — PagerDuty integration

- Notification channel in Cloud Monitoring
- Attach to alert policies; test incident
- See [docs/sre/oncall/test-alerts.md](../sre/oncall/test-alerts.md)

### 15 — Cloud Armor on storefront

- Security policy; OWASP CRS baseline
- Attach to boutique Ingress backend service
- Test blocked vs allowed request (optional curl with bad pattern)

### 16 — Smoke validation + SRE artifacts

- Full checklist: HTTPS, policies, SLOs live, runbooks exist, alert test, dig/curl
- Verify production bar from project description
- Link game day and on-call next steps

